# Generated or vendored - never hand-formatted, and reformatting them produces
# enormous diffs that bury real changes. `wp-scripts format` defaults to the
# whole project, so without this a single run rewrote 56,000 lines of
# package-lock.json plus every workflow and config file.

# Lockfiles. Regenerated by their package manager; formatting them guarantees
# a conflict on the next install and gains nothing.
package-lock.json
composer.lock

# Dependencies and build output
node_modules/
vendor/
build/
blocks/build/
test-results/
playwright-report/

# Machine-owned. release-please rewrites these, and Renovate rewrites
# renovate.json's schema on its own schedule.
CHANGELOG.md
.release-please-manifest.json

# CI definitions. Prettier reflows YAML in ways that fight the comments these
# carry, and GitHub Actions has its own conventions.
.github/workflows/

# WordPress.org readme is not Markdown; prettier mangles its header block.
readme.txt
